# Privacy Policy — Combinado

_Last updated: November 22, 2026_

Combinado is the app for people who work for themselves: it makes the quote, organizes the schedule
and the jobs, collects payment and issues the receipt, all on the phone. It was made to work with no
account, no server and no internet: **what you enter stays on your phone**. This policy explains
what the app uses, why, and what happens on the free plan, which shows ads.

## 1. What stays on your phone

Your business details (name, logo, contact, tax ID and payment methods), clients, quotes, work
orders, receipts, payments, catalog, schedule, notes and receipts you keep, photos and your settings
are stored only on the device. PDFs, payment QR codes and receipts are created on the phone itself,
and reminders are scheduled on it. We have no server, create no account and never receive a copy of
this data. The database and the photos are kept out of the system's automatic cloud backup.

The clients you add are other people's data: they stay on the phone and only leave it if you send
them a document or include them in a backup or a spreadsheet.

## 2. Permissions

Each permission is requested only when you use the feature, and the app keeps working if you say
no. Combinado never asks for location or the calendar, and the app's camera never records sound.

| Permission | What for |
|---|---|
| Camera | Take a photo of a receipt, your logo and before and after photos of a job. The photo is kept in an app folder. |
| Photos | Pick a photo with the system photo picker: the app only sees the photos you pick. |
| Contacts | Import clients from the phone's contacts. They are read on the device and only the people you pick are added. |
| Notifications | Remind you of visits, quotes about to expire and payments due, at the time you choose. |
| Exact alarm (Android) | Remind you right on time, such as 1 hour before a visit. Without it, the reminder may be late. |
| Files | Save and open the backup and the spreadsheet, attach a receipt PDF and, with Premium, save the automatic backup copy, always through the system file picker. |

## 3. Documents, messages, backups and sharing

Something only leaves the device when you send it: a quote or receipt as a PDF, a message ready in
WhatsApp, a backup, the spreadsheet for your accountant or an email to support. The app never sends
anything on its own: it gets the message ready and you tap send. You choose where it goes (WhatsApp,
email, cloud, memory card); from then on, the policy of that service applies. Cost, margin and
profit never appear on the PDF or the receipt.

In an email to support, the device details (model and versions) are only included if you leave that
option on, never your clients' data or amounts, and the email is sent from your own email app.

## 4. Ads (free plan)

The free plan shows ads from **Google AdMob**. To show and measure ads, Google may collect the
device's advertising ID, the IP address (and the approximate location derived from it), technical
device and system details, and interactions with ads.

- Where the law requires it (such as the European Economic Area, the UK and Switzerland), the app
  asks for your consent first through Google's consent platform, and you can change your choice
  later.
- On iPhone, the system asks whether the app may track you across apps; without permission, the
  advertising ID is not used.
- Ad requests never include client data, amounts or photos.
- With **Premium** there are no ads and the ads SDK is not started.

How Google uses this data: <https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites>.

## 5. Purchases

Subscriptions and the lifetime purchase are processed by **Google Play** or the **App Store**. We
never receive your payment details; the app only asks the store whether Premium is active. The
payments you record from your clients, including by Pix, are only notes on the phone: the app never
moves money or connects to banks.

## 6. Internet

The app uses the internet only for ads (free plan) and the store (purchases and restore
purchases). Everything else works offline.

## 7. Children

The app is not directed to children under 13 and does not knowingly collect children's data.

## 8. Retention and deletion

Data stays on the phone until you delete it. What you delete goes to the Trash and stays there for
30 days before it is deleted for good; you can also delete it forever sooner. **Settings › Data ›
Erase all data** makes the app like new; uninstalling the app also deletes everything. Backups,
spreadsheets and documents you exported or sent stay wherever you saved them. Since we keep none of
your data, there is nothing to delete on our side; requests about ad data can be made to Google in
the ad settings of your account or device.

## 9. Your rights

You have the rights provided by the LGPD (Brazil), the GDPR (Europe) and similar laws. Write to us at
the email below with any question or request; we reply within 30 days.

## 10. Changes

If this policy changes, the date at the top is updated and relevant changes are announced in the app.

